// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/docker-image.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeDockerImage(path: "/recipes/docker-image", title: "Build a Docker image — Recipes", description: "Build a Docker image of a WebFluent site: one stage installs wf and builds, a second serves the build with nginx.") {
    RecipeShell("Build a Docker image", summary: "This recipe packs a WebFluent site into a Docker image that serves it with nginx, for a host that runs containers.  You need Docker on the machine that builds the image. The image installs `wf` itself, as [Install wf on a build machine](/recipes/install-wf-in-ci) shows.  Add a `Dockerfile` at the project's root:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "check-it", label: "Check it"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Install wf on a build machine", to: "/recipes/install-wf-in-ci"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Use environment values, and keep secrets out", to: "/recipes/environments-and-secrets"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/docker-image.md", how: true, hasVariations: true) {
        code {
            CodeBlock(#"FROM debian:stable-slim AS build
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y curl ca-certificates
RUN curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/master/install.sh | WF_VERSION=v6.0.0 bash
WORKDIR /site
COPY . .
RUN /root/.webfluent/bin/wf build

FROM nginx:alpine
COPY --from=build /site/build /usr/share/nginx/html"#, title: "dockerfile")
            Markdown("Build and run the image:")
            Terminal(lines: [
                        Line(command: "docker build -t site ."),
                        Line(command: "docker run -p 8080:80 site")
                    ])
        }
        variations {
            Markdown("To use the settings from [Serve a site with nginx](/recipes/serve-with-nginx), copy them into the second stage as `/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf`. When TLS ends in front of the container, write `listen 80;` in place of the `listen 443 ssl http2;` line. The second stage then reads:")

            CodeBlock(#"FROM nginx:alpine
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
COPY --from=build /site/build /usr/share/nginx/html"#, title: "dockerfile")

            Markdown("Here `nginx.conf` is that `server` block, beside the `Dockerfile`, with its `root` changed to `/usr/share/nginx/html`.")

        }
        Markdown("1. The first stage, `build`, installs `curl`, installs `wf` into `/root/.webfluent/bin/`, copies the project in and builds it to `/site/build`. `WF_VERSION` pins the release, so the image builds the same way until you change it.\n2. The second stage starts from `nginx:alpine` and copies only the built site into nginx's document root. `wf` and the project's sources stay behind in the first stage.\n3. `docker run -p 8080:80` serves the site on port 8080 of your machine.")

        Heading("Check it", id: "check-it").h2

        Markdown("Open `http://localhost:8080` and a deep link, and check the headers with `curl -I http://localhost:8080/`. Then go through [Check a deploy](/recipes/check-a-deploy).")

    }
}
